{
  "_comment": [
    "What the C# INFANTRY does, recorded by InfantryReferenceTests.MeasureTheInfantry.",
    "",
    "csharp-army.json carries n, z and spread for the riflemen and nothing else.",
    "Every quantity item 2 has argued over is an ARMOUR quantity, so the core's",
    "infantry - 72 of its 96 units a side - had never been held to anything. It",
    "has no rifleman-on-rifleman fire at all, and it keeps a hard 24 m floor",
    "between the two lines that this army does not have.",
    "",
    "Recorded before item (e), because (e) deletes Army.cs and with it every",
    "chance to ask. Same conditions as the army recording - flat, still, seam at",
    "z=0, no aircraft, seed 20260901, ninety seconds, sampled every five - and",
    "the bullInf/bearInf columns of the `line` pass reproduce",
    "csharp-army.json passes.core-size-reinforce to the digit, and `line-24-72`",
    "reproduces its top-level rows. That equality is the check that this is the",
    "same run and not a second one that merely looks like it.",
    "",
    "SUBSCRIBING TO AN EVENT IN THIS ARMY CHANGES THE RUN. Shot?.Invoke draws",
    "its miss scatter INSIDE the argument, so `?.` skips two Rand() calls when",
    "nobody listens and makes them when somebody does. The first version of this",
    "recording carried a shot counter and walked away from the stored rows from",
    "t=25, which is when the first shot is fired. CourierHit has the same shape",
    "and the courier pass listens to it anyway, because that is the game's own",
    "condition - Bootstrap wires it to TruckHealth.Damage - which is why that",
    "pass is a separate run and its positions are not the line pass's."
  ],
  "setup": {
    "seed": 20260901,
    "dt": 0.0166666,
    "durationSeconds": 90,
    "sampleSeconds": 5,
    "seam": "z = 0, flat ground, no trade flow",
    "air": "none",
    "rifleRange": 26.0,
    "rifleHitChance": 0.045,
    "rifleReloadSeconds": [
      2.5,
      4.5
    ],
    "rifleDamage": 1.0,
    "infantryHp": 1.0,
    "courierRange": 34.0,
    "courierRifleDamage": [
      1.5,
      3.5
    ],
    "courierTankDamage": [
      5.0,
      11.0
    ],
    "infantryReinforceSeconds": 2.5,
    "armourReinforceSeconds": 6.0,
    "heat": 0.0,
    "flow": 0.0,
    "crowding": "NONE for infantry. Army.Separate is called on Armour pairs only (Army.cs:325)."
  },
  "_findings": [
    "1. THE TWO LINES INTERPENETRATE. The closest opposing pair of riflemen is",
    "   4.7 to 19.2 m once the lines meet (5.5 to 16.5 at 24/72), and the mean",
    "   nearest enemy settles at 24.4 to 35.5 m. The core holds 24.0 m exactly, at",
    "   every sample of every seed, because army.js applies BACK_OFF_RANGE to",
    "   riflemen. The blast radius is 16, so that floor alone decides that no",
    "   bomb in the core can ever catch men from both sides.",
    "",
    "2. RIFLE FIRE KILLS 28 A ROUND at the core's own establishment - 15 bull",
    "   and 13 bear over ninety seconds at 12/36, and 90 at 24/72. The core",
    "   scores zero: its rifle fire targets the courier and nothing else.",
    "   Replacement hides all of it in the headcount, which never leaves 34-36",
    "   of 36, which is why the army recording could carry n and spread for",
    "   ninety seconds and still say nothing about it.",
    "",
    "3. 18 TO 50 RIFLEMEN of the ~70 alive have an enemy inside 26 m at any",
    "   sample, from t=25 on. Contact is never lost, the same way the armour's",
    "   never is.",
    "",
    "4. THE TRUCK IS SHOT BY TANKS, NOT BY RIFLEMEN, AND THAT IS NOT CLOSE.",
    "   A courier parked on the seam for ninety seconds takes 163 tank hits for",
    "   1271.7 points and 6 rifle hits for 13.9 - 99% of the damage from the",
    "   arm the core does not model at all. The core fires at the truck from",
    "   EVERY unit that has it inside 26 m, armour and infantry alike, for a",
    "   flat one point. Wrong source, wrong range (34 m for a tank), wrong",
    "   size. Truck damage is M1's, so this is not a decoration.",
    "",
    "5. A RIFLEMAN ALMOST NEVER SHOOTS THE TRUCK, and the reason is the",
    "   selection rule, not the range: he fires only when he already has an",
    "   enemy rifleman inside 26 m, and switches to the courier only if it is",
    "   CLOSER than that man (cd < d2, with Heat at zero). In a line that",
    "   interpenetrates there is nearly always someone nearer. Six hits in",
    "   ninety seconds, from a truck parked in the middle of the fight.",
    "",
    "6. THE TANK RATE IS STEADY: 163 hits over the ninety, about 1.8 a second",
    "   once the lines are in contact, 7.8 points a hit, with 7 to 18 tanks",
    "   inside CourierRange at any sample. A hundred-point truck standing here",
    "   is written off in the first ten seconds of contact."
  ],
